WEBVTT


00:00:39.761 --> 00:00:43.470
<i>TYSON: I was just a kid when
I first got to see Muhammad Ali.</i>


00:00:43.641 --> 00:00:46.519
<i>I saw the way
people looked up to him...</i>


00:00:46.681 --> 00:00:49.070
<i>... saw their smiling faces...</i>


00:00:49.241 --> 00:00:53.439
<i>... and I said to myself,
"That's what I wanna be.</i>


00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:56.035
<i>I wanna be champ of the world. "</i>


00:00:56.201 --> 00:00:58.351
HAIRLIP:
Wait up, Mikey.


00:01:02.881 --> 00:01:05.475
[SIREN WAILING IN THE DISTANCE]


00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.029
- Just give it...
- Shh!


00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.833
Freeze.


00:01:17.561 --> 00:01:21.031
- Don't shit in your drawers.
HAIRLIP: It's just Dog.


00:01:21.201 --> 00:01:23.396
Damn, man.
What took you so long?


00:01:23.561 --> 00:01:24.880
Hey.


00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.954
There they are.


00:01:31.241 --> 00:01:33.277
Go in there and do it.


00:01:33.921 --> 00:01:35.149
TITO:
Do it, man.


00:01:35.641 --> 00:01:38.155
Fuck them up, Mikey.


00:01:41.961 --> 00:01:43.917
Showtime.


00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:49.469
BO Y 1: All right, now this is me and you.
One on one.


00:01:49.641 --> 00:01:53.077
Now, clear it out.
Clear it out, clear it out.


00:01:53.241 --> 00:01:55.277
Clear it out.
I'm taking it to the hole.


00:01:55.441 --> 00:01:59.116
BO Y 2: All right man, go, go.
BO Y 1: Move over. Move over.


00:02:00.721 --> 00:02:02.473
All right.


00:02:04.481 --> 00:02:06.392
BO Y 2:
Move right around.


00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:08.514
BO Y 3:
You got it.


00:02:10.241 --> 00:02:13.039
- Yeah.
BO Y 2: Watch him.


00:02:13.841 --> 00:02:15.832
BO Y 1: Watch out! Watch out!
BO Y 3: Hey, get him!


00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:17.992
BO Y 2:
Go! Go!


00:02:18.761 --> 00:02:21.480
- Let's split!
BO Y 3: Come on, man!


00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:25.678
Shit. Shit!


00:02:26.921 --> 00:02:29.879
Hurry up, Tito! Come on!


00:02:35.041 --> 00:02:37.236
[BO YS SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY]


00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.475
WOMAN:
Somebody call the police!


00:02:59.481 --> 00:03:02.518
[MAN AND WOMAN SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY ON TV]


00:03:05.681 --> 00:03:07.956
TYSON:
Rodney, is Mom home?


00:03:08.641 --> 00:03:09.869
<i>MAN [ON TV]:
And my grey slacks.</i>


00:03:10.041 --> 00:03:11.440
<i>WOMAN: Go to the cleaners.
MAN: Yes.</i>


00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.512
<i>WOMAN: Why not let me take care
of these chores...</i>


00:03:13.681 --> 00:03:15.751
<i>... just as I have been for
the past 20 years?</i>


00:03:15.921 --> 00:03:17.513
<i>MAN: Has it been that long?
WOMAN: Yes.</i>


00:03:17.681 --> 00:03:19.034
<i>You two are going to be late.</i>


00:03:19.201 --> 00:03:20.998
<i>MAN:
We're hurrying, we're hurrying. Goodbye.</i>


00:03:21.161 --> 00:03:22.435
<i>WOMAN:
Goodbye, dear.</i>


00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.353
<i>- Bye, Mom.
- Bye, sweetie.</i>


00:03:24.521 --> 00:03:27.831
<i>Oh! Come home early.
I'm planning a surprise for tonight.</i>


00:03:35.241 --> 00:03:38.756
TYSON: Denise, is Mom home?
- Does it look like it?


00:03:51.441 --> 00:03:55.753
<i>JUDGE 1: Michael Gerald Tyson, you have
been found guilty of aggravated assault.</i>


00:03:55.921 --> 00:03:57.991
<i>JUDGE 2:
Public intoxication, vagrancy.</i>


00:03:58.161 --> 00:03:59.992
<i>JUDGE 3:
Guilty. Assault and battery.</i>


00:04:00.161 --> 00:04:02.436
<i>JUDGE 4: Possession of
a deadly weapon. Grand theft.</i>


00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.831
<i>JUDGE 2: Two counts of burglary.
JUDGE 3: Aggravated robbery.</i>


00:04:05.001 --> 00:04:07.595
<i>JUDGE 4: Guilty as charged.
JUDGE 1: Receipt of stolen goods.</i>


00:04:07.761 --> 00:04:09.991
<i>JUDGE 2: You have been found guilty...
JUDGE 4: Resisting arrest.</i>


00:04:10.161 --> 00:04:12.231
<i>...of strong-armed robbery.
JUDGE 3: Michael Tyson.</i>


00:04:12.401 --> 00:04:13.834
<i>JUDGE 1:
Assault with a deadly weapon.</i>


00:04:14.001 --> 00:04:16.561
<i>JUDGE 3: You will be incarcerated at
the Tryon School for Boys...</i>


00:04:16.721 --> 00:04:18.074
<i>... in Johnstown, upstate New York.</i>


00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:19.594
[GAVEL POUNDS]


00:04:27.201 --> 00:04:28.395
ROONEY:
What's this kid's name?


00:04:28.561 --> 00:04:30.631
ATLAS: How should I know?
ROONEY: You talked to Bobby.


00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:32.712
ATLAS:
He said he had a kid we should look at.


00:04:32.881 --> 00:04:33.996
CUS:
Not Bobby Stewart.


00:04:34.161 --> 00:04:35.992
ATLAS: Yeah, from the Tryon
detention facility.


00:04:36.161 --> 00:04:39.073
CUS: Great. That's all we need,
another juvenile delinquent.


00:04:40.841 --> 00:04:41.956
ROONEY:
What did this kid do?


00:04:42.121 --> 00:04:45.875
What didn't he do? Arrested something
like 40 times before he turned 12.


00:04:46.041 --> 00:04:47.997
Forty times? Jeez!


00:04:48.161 --> 00:04:50.675
Even Al Capone
wasn't arrested no 40 times.


00:04:50.841 --> 00:04:52.797
- Uh-oh. Sounds like a baddie.
ATLAS: No shit.


00:04:52.961 --> 00:04:55.350
- Don't he got a mother?
- Of course he's got a mother.


00:04:55.521 --> 00:04:58.638
There comes a point even
a mother's gotta toss in the towel.


00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.315
Bobby don't expect me to take this kid
into my home, does he?


00:05:01.481 --> 00:05:05.360
Look, Bobby don't expect nothing.
All he said was take a look at him.


00:05:07.721 --> 00:05:09.040
You all right, Cus?


00:05:09.201 --> 00:05:11.874
Yeah, fine. Go ahead, go ahead.
I'll catch up with you.


00:05:12.041 --> 00:05:13.679
ATLAS:
Come on, Kevin.


00:05:24.881 --> 00:05:26.678
[BOXERS GRUNTING]


00:05:38.281 --> 00:05:42.160
- That him?
BARANSKl: Five-nine, 180 pounds.


00:05:42.321 --> 00:05:43.913
That's him.


00:05:44.481 --> 00:05:45.960
[BOTH GRUNTING]


00:05:53.281 --> 00:05:54.555
CUS:
Strong.


00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:57.110
ROONEY: Yeah, I was expecting
some scrawny little punk.


00:05:57.281 --> 00:05:59.636
Jesus, what have you been
feeding them kids, Bobby?


00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:02.474
The usual,
steroids and Cocoa Puffs.


00:06:02.681 --> 00:06:04.080
[CHUCKLES]


00:06:08.961 --> 00:06:11.953
Not much for style, but Jesus,
he can hit.


00:06:13.641 --> 00:06:17.270
Fucking A he can hit. A goddamn kid
hitting like Joe Frazier.


00:06:19.521 --> 00:06:21.671
He's faster than shit.


00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:26.519
CUS:
Take it easy a second.


00:06:27.521 --> 00:06:30.831
- What's your name, son?
TYSON: Mike.


00:06:31.001 --> 00:06:32.957
Mike what?


00:06:33.401 --> 00:06:35.232
TYSON:
Mike Tyson.


00:06:38.081 --> 00:06:40.072
Mike Tyson.


00:06:40.241 --> 00:06:42.471
Well, go ahead.
Do what you're doing.


00:06:46.161 --> 00:06:49.870
- So, what do you think?
- What do I think?


00:06:50.561 --> 00:06:54.600
I think he hits with bad intentions,
that's what I think.


00:06:55.001 --> 00:06:56.559
[BOTH GRUNTING]


00:06:59.321 --> 00:07:01.118
TYSON:
Come on, come on.


00:07:01.441 --> 00:07:02.840
[HORN HONKING]
[TYRES SCREECH]


00:07:03.001 --> 00:07:04.719
MAN:
Jerk!


00:07:06.241 --> 00:07:10.917
There you go.
This is our side over here.


00:07:11.081 --> 00:07:12.992
Now, back to what I was saying.


00:07:13.161 --> 00:07:18.155
Oh, yeah. Don't worry about
being scared and going into a fight.


00:07:18.321 --> 00:07:20.960
It's when you ain't scared,
that's the time to worry.


00:07:21.121 --> 00:07:24.318
Fear is the friend of every good
and reasonable athlete. Slow up.


00:07:25.001 --> 00:07:29.279
Yeah, you see that house over there?
That's your new home, Mike.


00:07:34.281 --> 00:07:36.954
MAN: Hey, Cus.
CUS: Make a right here. A right!


00:07:38.041 --> 00:07:41.954
Careful. Now, here we are.


00:07:49.041 --> 00:07:53.239
Come on in.
Make yourself at home. Camille!


00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:55.996
I want you to meet this woman.


00:07:58.201 --> 00:07:59.350
Come here.


00:07:59.521 --> 00:08:02.274
Say hello to Mike. Mike's a fighter.


00:08:02.441 --> 00:08:03.954
Come on.


00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:10.037
Mike, this is Camille Ewald.


00:08:12.041 --> 00:08:15.351
- Say, "Pleased to meet you."
- Pleased to meet you, ma'am.


00:08:17.561 --> 00:08:19.199
CAMILLE:
Hmph.


00:08:19.361 --> 00:08:20.999
It's all right.


00:08:26.401 --> 00:08:29.393
Now, don't get sore.
I know it's another mouth to feed...


00:08:29.561 --> 00:08:33.076
...but we could use that extra
200 bucks a month around here.


00:08:34.161 --> 00:08:36.516
Come on, I'll show you to your room.


00:08:43.721 --> 00:08:47.919
TYSON: Is Camille your wife?
- Not exactly. It's her house.


00:08:48.081 --> 00:08:49.594
I don't think she wants me here.


00:08:49.761 --> 00:08:53.595
CUS: What, that?
Aw, she's just a little shy, that's all.


00:08:54.641 --> 00:08:57.997
Will you look at this? I tell you,
if I catch the bum who did this...


00:08:58.161 --> 00:09:00.959
...he's gonna be a couple teeth
short of a smile, believe me.


00:09:01.121 --> 00:09:03.476
See, I got a half a dozen fighters
staying here.


00:09:03.641 --> 00:09:05.438
It's important that
everybody be neat.


00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:10.277
Now, this will be your room here.
We gotta get you an alarm clock.


00:09:13.561 --> 00:09:15.756
Who ate my ice cream?


00:09:16.321 --> 00:09:20.519
Don't you ever let me catch you
eating my ice cream! Not never!


00:09:33.321 --> 00:09:36.358
What's the difference
between a hero and a coward?


00:09:37.321 --> 00:09:41.872
There ain't no difference.
Inside, they're both exactly alike.


00:09:42.041 --> 00:09:44.601
Both scared of dying or getting hurt.


00:09:44.761 --> 00:09:49.471
But it's what the hero does
that makes him a hero.


00:09:49.641 --> 00:09:53.839
It's what the other guy doesn't do
that makes him a coward.


00:09:54.001 --> 00:09:55.559
[DOOR CLOSES]


00:10:04.841 --> 00:10:07.196
[ALARM CLOCK RINGING]


00:10:14.001 --> 00:10:15.912
Shit.


00:10:29.081 --> 00:10:33.836
<i>CUS: When two men step into a ring,
one and only one deserves to win.</i>


00:10:34.001 --> 00:10:37.630
<i>When you step in the ring,
you gotta know you deserve to win.</i>


00:10:38.601 --> 00:10:40.512
<i>You gotta know destiny
owes you victory...</i>


00:10:40.681 --> 00:10:43.115
<i>... because you trained harder
than your opponent.</i>


00:10:43.281 --> 00:10:48.719
<i>You sparred harder. You ran farther.
You see, you got up earlier.</i>


00:10:49.521 --> 00:10:53.514
I know you ain't sleeping.
I know you can hear me.


00:11:00.481 --> 00:11:04.235
Always keep your chin
tucked down into your chest.


00:11:04.401 --> 00:11:07.552
I don't care if you're running roadwork,
or walking around school...


00:11:07.721 --> 00:11:10.189
...or watching TV,
keep that chin tucked down...


00:11:10.361 --> 00:11:13.558
...and your eyes looking up and out.


00:11:15.601 --> 00:11:20.038
CUS: One word describes
Rocky Marciano: Tenacity.


00:11:20.201 --> 00:11:23.079
Only 187 pounds,
but to this day...


00:11:23.241 --> 00:11:26.278
...he remains the only
undefeated heavyweight champion.


00:11:26.441 --> 00:11:27.510
How?


00:11:27.681 --> 00:11:30.479
Because he wouldn't imagine
that he could lose.


00:11:30.641 --> 00:11:35.556
He would never even allow the concept
of defeat to enter his mind.


00:11:38.201 --> 00:11:41.830
Don't watch gloves.
Watch the chest.


00:11:42.001 --> 00:11:43.912
You wait for a glove to move,
you're dead.


00:11:44.081 --> 00:11:46.276
When the chest flexes, you bob.


00:11:53.121 --> 00:11:55.794
CUS: Joe Louis may have been
quiet on the outside...


00:11:55.961 --> 00:11:58.953
...but on the inside,
he was pure rage.


00:11:59.121 --> 00:12:01.635
He was a Negro in a white
man's world, and he hated it.


00:12:02.201 --> 00:12:05.398
Up and down the street,
24 hours a day.


00:12:24.041 --> 00:12:25.872
CUS:
Staying in constant motion.


00:12:26.041 --> 00:12:28.509
Your head ain't never again
where he last seen it.


00:12:28.681 --> 00:12:31.718
You give him a target, and by
the time he swings, it ain't there.


00:12:31.881 --> 00:12:36.033
And when you move, counter.
Ha! Five to the ribs, huh? Ha! Ha!


00:12:36.201 --> 00:12:38.999
- Four-one upstairs. Got it?
- Okay.


00:12:39.161 --> 00:12:40.879
All right, here we go.


00:12:41.521 --> 00:12:44.354
If you don't get hit, you don't lose.
It's as simple as that.


00:12:44.521 --> 00:12:47.115
Once you learn to stay low
and tuck behind your gloves...


00:12:47.281 --> 00:12:52.036
...in constant motion, no one's
gonna be able to land nothing.


00:12:54.441 --> 00:12:58.719
Lies and deceit. Subterfuge,
that's what we deal in.


00:12:58.881 --> 00:13:01.679
Don't ever let anyone
know your real intentions.


00:13:02.521 --> 00:13:05.240
CUS:
Champion fighters are champion liars.


00:13:05.401 --> 00:13:06.436
Best in the world.


00:13:06.601 --> 00:13:08.796
<i>ALI [ON FILM]: Keep your camera moving
because I'm kind of fast.</i>


00:13:08.961 --> 00:13:09.996
[GRUNTING]


00:13:10.161 --> 00:13:12.311
<i>Back off of him, just keep boxing.</i>


00:13:13.081 --> 00:13:15.390
Who ate my ice cream?


00:13:16.521 --> 00:13:18.955
Who ate my ice cream?


00:13:21.601 --> 00:13:23.910
Who ate my ice cream, damn it?


00:13:31.321 --> 00:13:33.232
[TYSON CRYING]


00:13:39.241 --> 00:13:40.799
ATLAS:
Mike.


00:13:45.441 --> 00:13:46.920
ROONEY:
What's up?


00:13:47.081 --> 00:13:49.754
- Mike's mom passed away.
- Oh, jeez.


00:13:50.201 --> 00:13:52.840
CUS: He's gotta take a bus to Brooklyn.
Drive him into town.


00:13:53.001 --> 00:13:54.559
ROONEY:
Sure.


00:14:39.761 --> 00:14:41.911
What you gonna do, Mike?


00:14:43.361 --> 00:14:45.670
You gonna move back home here?


00:14:46.641 --> 00:14:48.757
No, man, I got a home.


00:14:49.281 --> 00:14:51.670
[SIREN WAILING IN THE DISTANCE]


00:15:04.161 --> 00:15:05.560
[HAMMERING]


00:15:23.481 --> 00:15:25.233
Hi, Mike.


00:15:26.521 --> 00:15:29.831
- Hey, Jamie.
- What are you doing?


00:15:30.361 --> 00:15:31.589
Building a pigeon coop.


00:15:33.601 --> 00:15:35.671
I heard about your mom.


00:15:35.841 --> 00:15:37.479
ATLAS:
Hey, Mike.


00:15:39.561 --> 00:15:41.279
Glad to have you back home.


00:15:43.761 --> 00:15:45.080
Jamie.


00:15:45.241 --> 00:15:48.916
Okay, Uncle Teddy. I gotta go.


00:15:53.361 --> 00:15:55.272
Pigeons, huh?


00:15:59.161 --> 00:16:02.153
My old man used to call them
flying rats.


00:16:03.961 --> 00:16:05.792
So how was the funeral?


00:16:07.681 --> 00:16:09.239
Yeah.


00:16:09.681 --> 00:16:11.160
Mike...


00:16:13.201 --> 00:16:14.998
Do you know what a professional is?


00:16:17.241 --> 00:16:20.233
- Somebody who gets paid to...
- It's got nothing to do with money.


00:16:22.641 --> 00:16:26.793
A professional is a guy who performs
no matter what he's feeling inside.


00:16:26.961 --> 00:16:27.996
You understand me?


00:16:28.481 --> 00:16:30.073
No matter what.


00:16:32.441 --> 00:16:33.840
Here.


00:16:36.761 --> 00:16:39.195
TYSON: What is it?
- It's yours.


00:16:39.921 --> 00:16:42.515
Muhammad Ali gave it to me,
and I'm giving it to you.


00:16:42.681 --> 00:16:45.639
Take it with you
to the Junior Olympics.


00:16:54.601 --> 00:16:55.954
[BELL DINGS]


00:17:00.521 --> 00:17:03.194
<i>ANNOUNCER [OVER PA]:
In the heavyweight position, we have...</i>


00:17:10.001 --> 00:17:13.676
ATLAS:
Come on, Mike, relax. Take it easy.


00:17:14.721 --> 00:17:18.270
- Teddy, I'm so scared.
- What are you scared of?


00:17:20.041 --> 00:17:23.351
- Letting Cus down.
- You ain't gonna let no one down.


00:17:23.521 --> 00:17:26.718
You fought tougher guys than this.
Look at your opponent there.


00:17:26.881 --> 00:17:28.394
Look at him.


00:17:32.281 --> 00:17:35.114
You don't think he ain't scared?
Of course he is.


00:17:35.561 --> 00:17:36.835
Come on, what does Cus say?


00:17:37.001 --> 00:17:39.720
You remember what he said
about your fear? What did he say?


00:17:39.881 --> 00:17:42.395
- To... To use it.
- Use it how?


00:17:42.561 --> 00:17:44.791
- To turn my fear into fire.
- That's right.


00:17:44.961 --> 00:17:47.680
So, what are you gonna do
when you get in that ring?


00:17:49.361 --> 00:17:52.990
I'm gonna open up with some sevens.
Seven.


00:17:53.161 --> 00:17:55.880
There you go. Chin down, eyes up.
Then what you gonna do?


00:17:56.041 --> 00:17:58.430
Two. Send a two.


00:17:58.601 --> 00:18:00.592
- And what's the next punch?
- Five.


00:18:00.761 --> 00:18:02.080
Seven, two, five.


00:18:02.241 --> 00:18:04.471
Seven, two, five.
Keep moving inside.


00:18:04.641 --> 00:18:06.233
And what are you gonna do inside?


00:18:06.401 --> 00:18:09.234
I'm gonna open up
like a son of a bitch.


00:18:10.201 --> 00:18:12.635
ATLAS:
All right. Let's go win a fight.


00:18:31.521 --> 00:18:32.510
[BELL DINGS]


00:18:32.681 --> 00:18:33.796
REFEREE:
Go!


00:18:37.761 --> 00:18:39.513
[BOXER GRUNTING]


00:18:40.241 --> 00:18:41.913
REFEREE:
Get in the corner!


00:18:42.641 --> 00:18:45.235
Four! Five!


00:18:45.401 --> 00:18:51.397
Six! Seven! Eight! Nine!


00:18:52.041 --> 00:18:54.111
- Ten!
TYSON: Yeah!


00:18:54.281 --> 00:18:56.590
ATLAS:
You did it, champ.


00:19:03.641 --> 00:19:07.077
DOCTOR: That's it. Just stay still.
Just stay still. Don't... Don't move.


00:19:07.241 --> 00:19:09.596
TRAINER: Will he be all right?
DOCTOR: He'll be fine.


00:19:09.841 --> 00:19:13.151
Eight? What do you mean eight?
They only do three rounds in the juniors.


00:19:13.321 --> 00:19:17.155
<i>ATLAS: No, no, eight seconds.
- Eight seconds!</i>


00:19:17.961 --> 00:19:20.270
What... What did he do,
shoot the guy?


00:19:20.441 --> 00:19:23.114
Might as well have.
They say it's a new record.


00:19:23.281 --> 00:19:24.919
It's all anyone's talking about.


00:19:25.081 --> 00:19:26.833
Well, where is he now?


00:19:27.001 --> 00:19:29.435
He's still in the ring.
They just announced it.


00:19:29.601 --> 00:19:32.434
